>> title: Whole Roasted Branzino with Citrus and Herbs
>> servings: 2
>> time: 35 minutes
>> tags: centerpiece, watchme, fish, oven, technique

Pat @whole branzino{2} dry inside and outside with #paper towels{}.

Score each fish three times per side with a #chef's knife{}.

Season cavities and skin with @kosher salt{1.5%tsp}, @black pepper{1/2%tsp}, and @olive oil{2%tbsp}.

-- watch: Citrus and herbs fill the cavity loosely without bulging it open.
Stuff each cavity with @lemon slices{6}, @parsley sprigs{6}, and @fennel fronds{1/2%cup}.

Roast on a #sheet pan{} at 425°F for ~{18%minutes}.

-- watch: Skin is blistered and flesh near the backbone flakes when nudged.
Check the fish at the thickest point with a #fork{}.

-- watch: Top fillet lifts cleanly from the bones in one broad piece.
Use a #fish spatula{} and #spoon{} to lift fillets from the skeleton.

Serve with @lemon wedges{} and @olive oil{}.
